It took me a very long time before I learned to play where I often
encountered nymphs still asleep.  Far more than just not kicking down
doors until you have explored as much of the level as possible.

I eventually figured out that my pet was exploring levels separately
from me and attacking sleeping nymphs.  There's an art to moving
through corridors with your pet behind you so yuo lead the exploration
but moving through rooms with your pet ahead of you so they thin the
crowds and kill about as many monsters as you do to balance
advancement between you and yout pet.

Now I enter a room, move to where I can fire on the nymph, start the
barrage, kill her as she moves towards me.  Does not work every time but
it sure works much better than having no idea where my pet went and
suddenly a nymph emerges from a corridor two squares away.  Which is
what happened to me all the time when I was a newer player.

In fact I originally learned the idea in games where I lost my pet to
the watch captain's long sword in mine town so I just started exploring
on my own.  Huh, without a pet I found all sorts of sleeping nymphs. 
Which cycles me back to the art of leading in a corridor, following in a
room.


